    "evidence_text": "PCNA functions as a molecular platform to trigger Cdt1 destruction and prevent re-replication\n\nUbiquitin-dependent protein degradation.\n\nKey role of Ubc5 and lysine-63 polyubiquitination in viral activation of IRF3.\n\nThe activation of IRF3 also requires two ubiquitin-binding domains of NEMO.\n\nUbiquitination on nonlysine residues by a viral E3 ubiquitin ligase.\n\nUbiquitination controls a broad range of cellular functions.\n\nThus, ubiquitination can occur on proteins lacking accessible lysines or an accessible N terminus.\n\nModification of proteins by SUMO is essential for the maintenance of genome integrity.\n\nYet how the activity of the SUMO ligase is controlled remains unknown.\n\nDNA damage tolerance during eukaryotic replication is orchestrated by PCNA ubiquitination.\n\nHowever, whether this interaction promotes fork remodeling and template switching in vivo was unknown.\n\nTargeting these fork protection systems represents a promising strategy to potentiate cancer chemotherapy.\n\nThe anaphase promoting complex/cyclosome: a machine designed to destroy\n\nAttachment of the ubiquitin-related protein Urm1p to the antioxidant protein Ahp1p.\n\nUrm1p conjugation has been implicated in the budding process and in nutrient sensing.",
